+The highest-value changes are the following five editorial tasks. The times are estimates for a writer already familiar with these files. They exclude implementation repairs and new proofs.
+
+First, spend two hours correcting the claims that are falsified by the inspected definitions. Narrow demand-only failure to successfully prepared bodies. Record the long-reason counterexample for the implementation lane. Restore context, signature and guard-observation premises. Replace insert-only with non-retractable. Separate slot predicates from object-contract claims. Fix the repair citation and the cellPackage sentence. These edits prevent a reader from building a false model.
+
+Second, spend three hours reducing the opening example to the contextual counter. Publish the literal package with its substitution recipe. Explain G's role. Show the absent-row pin, revocation, blocked field, successful choose and next bump. Label discarded refusal probes. Add one nonempty-context filling. This gives the semantics an example that distinguishes its central mechanisms.
+
+Third, spend four hours replacing the theorem inventory's soundness summary with a compact derivation. State LibTy, value typing, environment typing, thunk typing and continuation typing. State step_sound and the induction yielding run_sound. State the separate extraction result. Explain the empty-hole-signature boundary and the preparation bridge. This supplies the proof structure the target reader came to inspect.
+
+Fourth, spend four hours formalizing the contextual pipeline in the notation already chosen. Define the observed view and structural support predicates. Give ordered selection and failure rules. Define usesVar, capture-avoiding substitution, factor and reembed. State preparation's work, size, provenance and typing checks as distinct premises. Give a repair transition with explicit method-authority and law premises. This makes a small independent model possible without pretending to prove history-level contextual integrity.
